typhoon patch on fm1-base: the radio's supplies set at boot (fm1_radio_power), and read back into its log
SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0 (a change to fm1-base's MPL-2.0 files)

What: device/main_fm1.c calls felucca-bsp's fm1_radio_power (patches/felucca-bsp/0002) at boot, after the rail raise,
the radio off, in builds with a radio (FM1B_BLE, FM1B_WIFI). device/radio.c's radio_begin logs the four registers
at every radio start ("pwr 0:FB 7:A5 8:96 74:C0": V15's values), so a start that still fails says whether they took.
Why: Bluetooth's start crashed after a power cycle (typhoon, 2026-10-24; the cause and the values:
patches/felucca-bsp/0002).
Applies to: fm1-base ced9443. Needs patches/felucca-bsp/0002.
Upstream: not offered yet (charlesvestal/fm1-base).

diff --git a/device/main_fm1.c b/device/main_fm1.c
index c31647b..1eda7eb 100644
--- a/device/main_fm1.c
+++ b/device/main_fm1.c
@@ -746,6 +746,11 @@ static void fm1_main(void)
                                                     /* then 1.38 V (fm1_sys.h). At the boot loader's, flash fetches
                                                      * come back corrupted under load: the radio's trim crashed
                                                      * CTL-1 0.6 s into most Bluetooth starts */
+#if FM1B_BLE || FM1B_WIFI
+        fm1_radio_power();                          /* and the radio's DC-DC as V15 leaves it: after a power-on the
+                                                     * 1.3 V supply runs from its LDO and sags in the radio's trim, and
+                                                     * the start crashes (felucca-bsp fm1_sys.h fm1_radio_power) */
+#endif
         fm1_clock_read(clock_boot);
         clock_fix = (int8_t)fm1_clock_stock();      /* the stock 360 MHz, whichever bootloader started us (fm1_clock.h) */
         flash_ok = FL_FAR(fl_jedec_ram)() == 0x856014u;   /* the expected 1 MiB part, else RAM only */
diff --git a/device/radio.c b/device/radio.c
index eba0d3d..f36e4d6 100644
--- a/device/radio.c
+++ b/device/radio.c
@@ -319,6 +319,25 @@ static void radio_begin(const char *what)
     radio_t0 = shim_ms();
     radio_starting = 1;
     shim_log(what);
+    {                                             /* the radio's supplies, read back (fm1_radio_power at boot: V15's
+                                                   * values are 0:FB 7:A5 8:96 74:C0) */
+        static const uint8_t R[4] = {FM1_P3_ANA_CON0, FM1_P3_ANA_CON7, FM1_P3_ANA_CON8, FM1_P3_WLDO12_AUTO};
+        static const char H[] = "0123456789ABCDEF";
+        char b[32] = "pwr", *q = b + 3;
+        uint32_t i;
+        for (i = 0; i < 4u; i++) {
+            const uint8_t v = fm1_p33_read(R[i]);
+            *q++ = ' ';
+            if (R[i] >= 0x10u)
+                *q++ = H[R[i] >> 4];
+            *q++ = H[R[i] & 15u];
+            *q++ = ':';
+            *q++ = H[v >> 4];
+            *q++ = H[v & 15u];
+        }
+        *q = 0;
+        shim_log(b);
+    }
     radio_quiet = 1;
 #if BLE_MASK_AT_START
     {
